Now add regression tests. Create `test/invalid-utf8-storage.test.ts` following corrupt-storage.test.ts patterns. Cases:

1. Invalid UTF-8 bytes in title / description / scenario of a stored record (each of three invalid forms: lone continuation byte 0x80, truncated multibyte E4 B8 at end of string, overlong C0 AF / surrogate ED A0 80).
2. Bytes placed so that after replacement the record would still be structurally complete and JSON valid — must still fail.
3. Invalid bytes in other fields (id, createdAt) → fail.
4. GET → 500 {error:'unable to read ideas'}; POST valid → 500 {error:'无法读取已有意见数据，未保存新意见'}, no idea; disk byte-identical, no .tmp; restart still fails.
5. User-written "�" (EF BF BD) in stored data → readable as normal text, GET 200 with the char intact; POST succeeds.
6. Valid empty list unaffected (covered elsewhere, skip).

Write file as bytes: construct JSON with placeholder and splice in raw bytes, or build Buffer directly. Simplest: build the JSON string with a unique placeholder like "BADBYTE" and replace with Buffer.concat. Or write JSON.stringify of an array containing a placeholder string, then buffer-replace the placeholder with raw bytes.

E.g.:

```ts
function writeCorrupt(file: string, rawBytes: number[], field: 'title'|'description'|'scenario'|'id'|'createdAt') {
  const idea = { id:'bad-utf8-1', title:'标题', description:'正文', scenario:'场景', createdAt:'2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z' };
  idea[field] = '前缀\u0000BADBYTES\u0000后缀'; // hmm
}
```

Better: build with a marker string `@@BAD@@` inside the field value, JSON.stringify, then find marker bytes and replace with raw bytes via Buffer.concat.

```ts
function ideasFileWithBadBytes(badBytes: Buffer, field: string): Buffer {
  const idea: Record<string,string> = {
    id: 'bad-utf8-1',
    title: '正常标题',
    description: '正常正文',
    scenario: '正常场景',
    createdAt: '2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z',
  };
  idea[field] = '前缀@@BAD@@后缀';
  const json = Buffer.from(`${JSON.stringify([idea], null, 2)}\n`, 'utf8');
  const marker = Buffer.from('@@BAD@@', 'utf8');
  const at = json.indexOf(marker);
  return Buffer.concat([json.subarray(0, at), badBytes, json.subarray(at + marker.length)]);
}
```

Note: replacement with "�" would still be valid JSON and complete record — exactly the case described.

Bad byte cases:
- lone continuation: [0x80]
- truncated multibyte: [0xE4, 0xB8] (missing third byte of 中） — but careful: followed by '"' (0x22), which is not a continuation, so E4 B8 22 is invalid. Good.
- overlong C0 AF, surrogate ED A0 80, out-of-range F5 80 80 80, lone 0xFF.

Fields: title, description, scenario, plus id and createdAt ("即使问题位于其他已保存字段").

Also a case with invalid bytes in JSON whitespace/structure outside strings? Spec says "或替换后仍能组成完整意见，也应拒绝整份数据" — focus on fields. Maybe also invalid byte outside any string (e.g., between records) — replacement would make invalid JSON anyway, which already failed. Not needed but cheap to include? Keep to spec: fields including non-text positions. I'll include id and createdAt.

Tests per case: GET 500, POST 500 with error, no idea, disk byte-identical, no .tmp, restart still 500 and bytes unchanged.

Also positive test: stored "�" (EF BF BD) written by user → GET 200, content preserved verbatim; POST 201 succeeds and old record preserved byte-content (after save, the file will be rewritten with the new idea — the old record's text should be preserved as data, compare parsed). Also Chinese/emoji/newlines in stored data read fine (covered by legacy tests, but a small check with � is the key one).

Also test that a rejected POST doesn't leave temp file and doesn't modify bytes — included.

